<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yağıbasan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1164">1164</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yağıbasan was a Danishmendid emir, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gumustekin-gazi">Gümüştekin Gazi</a>, who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a> from about 1142 to 1164. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum and supported rivals of the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-ii">Kilij Arslan II</a>. His death in 1164 split the dynasty among competing heirs, allowing the Seljuks to absorb its lands by 1178.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yagibasan.jpg" alt="Yağıbasan" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danishmendids_(Sivas)._Nizam_al-Din_Yaghi_Basan._AH_536-559_(AD_1142-1164)_Sivas_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
